 &quot;the way it should have been built&quot;, &quot;refactor toward intent&quot;.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.pi/agent/skills/zero-tech-debt/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>anti-ui-slop</name>\n    <description>Stop coding agents from shipping generic UI. Use UIZZE&apos;s 800,000+ real web and iOS screens to build product-specific interfaces, define a design contract, cover required states, and run a hard finish gate. Use when designing, implementing, redesigning, critiquing, or pre-ship reviewing a web or iOS interface in Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, or another coding agent. Trigger with &quot;anti-ui-slop&quot;, &quot;stop UI slop&quot;, &quot;ground this UI in real screens&quot;, or &quot;run the UI finish gate&quot;.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/anti-ui-slop/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>archify</name>\n    <description>Create polished, validated architecture, workflow, sequence, data-flow, and lifecycle/state diagrams as explorable standalone HTML with inline SVG, dark/light themes, optional trace motion, and PNG/JPEG/WebP/SVG/WebM export. Accept plain-language requirements or pasted Mermaid flowchart, sequenceDiagram, and stateDiagram input; inspect repository evidence when the diagram must reflect real code. Use when the user asks to visualize system architecture, infrastructure, cloud/security/network topology, technical workflows, API call sequences, request lifecycles, data pipelines, ETL/ELT, data lineage, state machines, or to convert/beautify Mermaid.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/archify/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>codebase-design</name>\n    <description>Shared vocabulary for designing deep modules. Use when the user wants to design or improve a module&apos;s interface, find deepening opportunities, decide where a seam goes, make code more testable or AI-navigable, or when another skill needs the deep-module vocabulary.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/codebase-design/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>diagnosing-bugs</name>\n    <description>Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says &quot;diagnose&quot;/&quot;debug this&quot;, or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>domain-modeling</name>\n    <description>Build and sharpen a project&apos;s domain model. Use when discussing codebase terminology, writing or editing a CONTEXT.md, or recording or editing an ADR.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>done-means-done</name>\n    <description>Complete substantial authorized assignments with a persistent requirements ledger, mandatory remediation of every confirmed defect discovered in the project, executable acceptance evidence, final integration review, and recovery after interruption. Use for implementation, multi-step plans, exhaustive repairs, multiple deliverables, unfinished assignments, or requests to finish everything without repeated continue prompts. Restore the same task when resuming; never substitute a smaller assignment or call partial work complete.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/done-means-done/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>git-guardrails-claude-code</name>\n    <description>Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/git-guardrails-claude-code/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>grilling</name>\n    <description>Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any &apos;grill&apos; trigger phrases.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>migrate-to-shoehorn</name>\n    <description>Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/migrate-to-shoehorn/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>niblet</name>\n    <description>Keep interface work anchored to the product it belongs to instead of a generic template. Sets a short design contract, builds from the components and tokens already in the codebase, covers the states a surface can actually reach, and closes by looking at the rendered result. Use when building, reworking, or assessing a web or native interface. Trigger with &quot;niblet&quot;, &quot;niblet skill&quot;, &quot;niblet designer ui&quot;, or &quot;niblet review&quot;. Skip backend, CLI, data, and infrastructure work, prose-only tasks, and questions the product&apos;s own design system already settles.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/niblet/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>no-mistakes</name>\n    <description>Validate your code changes through the no-mistakes pipeline - automated code review, tests, lint, docs, push, PR, and CI - before they reach the configured push target. Use when the user asks to run no-mistakes, gate or ship or validate their changes, push safely, asks you to do a task and then validate it, or invokes /no-mistakes.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/no-mistakes/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail</name>\n    <description>Forces the laziest solution that actually works, simplest, shortest, most minimal. Channels a senior dev who has seen everything: question whether the task needs to exist at all (YAGNI), reach for the standard library before custom code, native platform features before dependencies, one line before fifty. Supports intensity levels: lite, full (default), ultra. Use on ANY coding task: writing, adding, refactoring, fixing, reviewing, or designing code, and choosing libraries or dependencies. Also use whenever the user says &quot;ponytail&quot;, &quot;be lazy&quot;, &quot;lazy mode&quot;, &quot;simplest solution&quot;, &quot;minimal solution&quot;, &quot;yagni&quot;, &quot;do less&quot;, or &quot;shortest path&quot;, or complains about over-engineering, bloat, boilerplate, or unnecessary dependencies. Do NOT use for non-coding requests (general knowledge, prose, translation, summaries, recipes).\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail-audit</name>\n    <description>Whole-repo audit for over-engineering. Like ponytail-review, but scans the entire codebase instead of a diff: a ranked list of what to delete, simplify, or replace with stdlib/native equivalents. Use when the user says &quot;audit this codebase&quot;, &quot;audit for over-engineering&quot;, &quot;what can I delete from this repo&quot;, &quot;find bloat&quot;, &quot;ponytail-audit&quot;, or &quot;/ponytail-audit&quot;. One-shot report, does not apply fixes.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail-audit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail-debt</name>\n    <description>Harvest every `ponytail:` comment in the codebase into a debt ledger, so the deliberate shortcuts and deferrals ponytail leaves behind get tracked instead of rotting into &quot;later means never&quot;. Use when the user says &quot;ponytail debt&quot;, &quot;/ponytail-debt&quot;, &quot;what did ponytail defer&quot;, &quot;list the shortcuts&quot;, &quot;ponytail ledger&quot;, or &quot;what did we mark to do later&quot;. One-shot report, changes nothing.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail-debt/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail-gain</name>\n    <description>Show ponytail&apos;s measured impact as a compact scoreboard: less code, less cost, more speed, from the benchmark medians. One-shot display, not a persistent mode, and not a per-repo number. Trigger: /ponytail-gain, &quot;ponytail gain&quot;, &quot;what does ponytail save&quot;, &quot;show ponytail impact&quot;, &quot;ponytail scoreboard&quot;.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail-gain/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail-help</name>\n    <description>Quick-reference card for all ponytail modes, skills, and commands. One-shot display, not a persistent mode. Trigger: /ponytail-help, &quot;ponytail help&quot;, &quot;what ponytail commands&quot;, &quot;how do I use ponytail&quot;.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail-help/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ponytail-review</name>\n    <description>Code review focused exclusively on over-engineering. Finds what to delete: reinvented standard library, unneeded dependencies, speculative abstractions, dead flexibility. One line per finding: location, what to cut, what replaces it. Use when the user says &quot;review for over-engineering&quot;, &quot;what can we delete&quot;, &quot;is this over-engineered&quot;, &quot;simplify review&quot;, or invokes /ponytail-review. Complements correctness-focused review, this one only hunts complexity.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/ponytail-review/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>prototype</name>\n    <description>Build a throwaway prototype to answer a design question. Use when the user wants to sanity-check whether a state model or logic feels right, or explore what a UI should look like.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/prototype/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>research</name>\n    <description>Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/research/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>resolving-merge-conflicts</name>\n    <description>Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/resolving-merge-conflicts/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>scaffold-exercises</name>\n    <description>Create exercise directory structures with sections, problems, solutions, and explainers that pass linting. Use when user wants to scaffold exercises, create exercise stubs, or set up a new course section.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/scaffold-exercises/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>setup-pre-commit</name>\n    <description>Set up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged (Prettier), type checking, and tests in the current repo. Use when user wants to add pre-commit hooks, set up Husky, configure lint-staged, or add commit-time formatting/typechecking/testing.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/setup-pre-commit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>source-command-de-sloppify</name>\n    <description>Migrated source command `de-sloppify`</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/source-command-de-sloppify/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>source-command-evolve</name>\n    <description>Migrated source command `evolve`</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/source-command-evolve/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>source-command-learn</name>\n    <description>Migrated source command `learn`</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/source-command-learn/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>source-command-learn-eval</name>\n    <description>Extract reusable patterns from the session, self-evaluate quality before saving, and determine the right save location (Global vs Project).</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/source-command-learn-eval/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>tdd</name>\n    <description>Test-driven development. Use when the user wants to build features or fix bugs test-first, mentions &quot;red-green-refactor&quot;, or wants integration tests.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/tdd/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-bug</name>\n    <description>Autonomous bug route of /to-goal: same control plane, worktree isolation, ledger, budgets, and review, with the route pinned to diagnosing-bugs and the bug fast path armed, so a reproducible bug goes red → regression test → fix → review → hand back without research, grilling, spec, or tickets unless the diagnosis proves it needs them. Use on /to-bug &lt;symptom | failing command | issue ref&gt; or $to-bug.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/to-bug/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-goal</name>\n    <description>Autonomous software-factory pipeline over the mattpocock/skills flow map plus research-stack, defensive-design, and zero-tech-debt: route, on-ramp, conditional research, self-answered grilling, to-spec, to-tickets, implement-spec task-graph build in parallel worktrees, code-review, retro, with no pauses. Use on /to-goal &lt;objective&gt; or $to-goal, when the user wants a feature or skill delivered fully autonomously, or under a loop.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/to-goal/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-new</name>\n    <description>Greenfield route of /to-goal: create a new project, package, service, or agent skill from nothing, autonomously. Creates the directory and repository when none exists, scaffolds a runnable baseline so the environment contract holds, researches stack and versions up front through research-stack, maps the effort with wayfinder, then runs the same grill → spec → tickets → build → review → retro pipeline on the same control plane. Use on /to-new &lt;thing to create&gt; or $to-new.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/to-new/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-orc</name>\n    <description>Delegation-only orchestrator: plan, dispatch, gate, and judge a task through four sequential phases (scouting → researching → implementing → verification), executing nothing yourself. Every worker is pi running zai/glm-5.3-flash at thinking max, dispatched through the pi-delegate relay, and every dispatch returns a machine-readable status the orchestrator judges instead of trusting prose. Ends with one raw JSON assessment (PASS / REVISE / FAIL). Use on /to-orc &lt;task&gt; or $to-orc, or when the user wants work delegated under strict phase control with an evidence-backed verdict.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/to-orc/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wizard</name>\n    <description>Generate an interactive bash wizard that walks a human through steps only they can perform. Use when provisioning infrastructure, setting up credentials or CI secrets, walking an unfamiliar third-party dashboard, or running a one-off migration or cutover. Don&apos;t invoke this for steps the agent can perform itself.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/wizard/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>writing-for-agents</name>\n    <description>Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.agents/skills/writing-for-agents/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>council-mode</name>\n    <description>Run a bounded supervisor-mediated advisor council. Use when the user asks for council mode, asks to convene advisors, debate a decision, cross-examine recommendations, or run /council.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/skills/council-mode/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>pi-subagents</name>\n    <description>Delegate to builtin or custom subagents for single-agent handoffs, parallel\nreview, scripted chaining, async work, forked context, and coordinated\nworkflows. Use when one parent agent should stay in control while children\nsupply focused context, planning, review, or execution.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/skills/pi-subagents/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>mcp-scripting</name>\n    <description>Write mcpScript JavaScript for discovering, inspecting, and calling MCP tools.</description>\n    <location>/Users/panda/Projects/open-source/tools/pi-mcp-adapter/skills/mcp-scripting/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\nCurrent working directory: /Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The conversation history before this point was compacted into the following summary:\n\n<summary>\n## Goal\nRebuild/reconstruct source code for `Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg` (macOS Electron app, Cursor-derived \"Grok Bot\" by Anysphere, codename \"sand\"), using the reference repo `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main` (a source-oriented reconstruction of Grok Bot 0.18.0) as the scaffold. Follow the 4-phase reverse-engineering workflow in the user's original prompt (mount/triage → tech stack → extraction → scaffold & reconstruction). User explicitly wants the rebuild driven to completion.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use subagents for scouting/analysis tasks (user preference; implementation done inline)\n- Evidence-only reconstruction rule (inherited from reference PROVENANCE.md): every recovered behavior needs an inspectable artifact anchor; no invented UI/features\n- Working dir: `~/Projects/test-local/grok-bot` (DMG, `analysis/`); new repo at `~/Projects/active/grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed/`\n- Node v24.19.0 installed; repo `engines` requires `>=26.5.0 <27` — install/run works fine with `npm ci --engine-strict=false`; env var renamed `GROK_BOT_018_APP` → `GROK_BOT_044_APP`\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- **Prior analysis exists** in `~/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/`: `RE-REPORT.md` (verdict: 0.44 is Cursor rebranded→x.ai Grok agent platform), `sections/sec-{main,daemon,coord,native,render}.md`, `extracted/` (0.44 asar contents, 41MB), `app.asar` (34,485,800 bytes), `app.asar.unpacked/dist/{native,deps}`\n- **4 scout findings** in `analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-{ref-anatomy,044-sources,delta-018-044,native-render}.md` (note: workflow's final `runs.all` step hit infra duplicate-key error but all children completed)\n- **Rebuild plan written**: `analysis/REBUILD-PLAN.md` (Phases A–D with strategy table)\n- **New repo created**: `~/Projects/active/grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed/` (rsync copy of reference, git init, 2 commits)\n- **Phase A complete, committed** (`b3f9c86`):\n  - `scripts/lib/config.mjs`: upstreamVersion=\"0.44.0\", dmgSha256=`020d6080b44a11c91cefe6ff11d0e30f993efa54991f8c1a4625653499c21420`, upstreamAsarSha256=`dbf2bbf4c8f870ccbae459eba9f84a84ba1c00aaa97ffbecbd806b3f0452ae1e`, dmgUrl pattern, output names → \"Grok Bot 0.44 …\"\n  - `scripts/lib/runtime.mjs`: hydrate required list = `dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `dist/node-agent-coordinator/main.cjs`, `dist/local-exec-daemon/main.cjs`, `dist/electron-preload/preload.cjs`, `dist/renderer/index.html` (0.44 has NO `dist/host/`); tempdir names → `grok-bot-044-`\n  - `scripts/bootstrap-runtime.mjs`: tempdir `grok-bot-044-mount-`, env `GROK_BOT_044_APP`\n  - `src/app/package.json` = 0.44.0 asar pkg (name \"sand\", 84 deps, +11/−5 vs 0.18: removed `@sand/dune`, `@sentry/node`, highlight.js, rehype-katex, undici; added canvas-shared, dune, grok-bot-harness, grok-bot-voice-call-harness, mcp-core, messages-mac, metrics, otel-proto, @lingui/*, @sentry/node-core)\n  - `src/app/dist/` hydrated (41MB, verified via `npm run bootstrap` end-to-end)\n  - `research-archives/original/0.44.0/`: real DMG (141,947,035 bytes) + `artifacts.json` (strict 4-key schema) + `SHA256SUMS`\n  - `PROVENANCE.md` rewritten for 0.44 (Electron 42.1.0 / Chrome 148.0.7778.97 — same shell as 0.18, ABI-identical; Anysphere DCNK4UB866)\n  - Root `package.json`/`package-lock.json` name/version → `grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed@0.44.0-reconstructed.1`; README env-var renamed\n  - Tests retargeted (`tests/research-archives.test.mjs` → 0.44 archiveRoot/version/1 artifact; `tests/publication-bootstrap.test.mjs` → new hydrate list); **18/18 pass**\n- **DMG mounted & verified**: bundle id `com.anysphere.sand`, CFBundleVersion 0.44.0, LSMinimumSystemVersion 12.0, Electron Framework 42.1.0/Chrome 148.0.7778.97\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] **Phase B: anchor/composition rework** — `scripts/verify.mjs` + `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs` `runtimeComposition` + packaging scripts still assume 0.18 asar layout. Just inspected `scripts/verify.mjs` lines 40–135. Deltas to absorb:\n  - `dist/host/{host-main.cjs, agent-isolation/*, extensions/*}` gone from upstream (host role folded into `dist/local-exec-daemon/main.cjs` 3.58MB)\n  - `dist/electron-preload/preload-dev-controls.cjs` absent (0.44 has only preload.cjs, preload-vnc.cjs, preload-webview.cjs)\n  - `dist/node-deps/tree-sitter*/...` → moved to `dist/deps/` (per `dist/deps/runtime-deps-manifest.json`: required=[cursor-proclist, tree-sitter, tree-sitter-bash])\n  - `app-icon-C7NKj2u7.png` + `frontend/manifests/renderer-runtime-assets.json` are 0.18-chunk-specific → need 0.44 icon record + inventory\n  - `dist/recovered-source/host/host-main.cjs` artifact-fallback needs 0.44 replacement\n  - Dev-seams/runtime-seams string anchors in `main-core.cjs` (1.73MB)/`main-app.cjs` (2.04MB) need re-derivation (minified, Sentry-wrapped, no sourcemaps)\n  - Renderer router/settings patch anchors: park initially — ship byte-for-byte 0.44 renderer\n- [ ] Phase C: source delta port (chrome-import-worker TS, voice-call harness, coordinator 98-method registry, 40-tool daemon, proto surface GrokBotService 136/SandBoxService 39/Dashboard 660/bc 226/Analytics 8 from `proto.cjs` 4.06MB, deep-link routes, CUGrokBotService sidecar, Temporal enums)\n- [ ] Phase D: `npm run package`, ad-hoc codesign, verify suite\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Scaffold = fork of 0.18 reconstruction**: whole custom Node packaging pipeline (bootstrap→esbuild→asar overlay→ad-hoc codesign, no electron-builder) transfers; only constants + anchors change\n- **Renderer mode = fidelity**: ship 0.44 `dist/renderer/` byte-for-byte (386 minified chunks, no sourcemaps; full TSX recovery = poor ROI); optional later diff-and-patch via reference's `recover-frontend.mjs`\n- **Native binaries opaque**: ship 0.44 `dist/native/{sand-webauthn-signer (Rust, 4.5MB), sand-op-launcher (136KB)}` + `dist/deps/*.node` as-is; Node-side TS drivers from 0.18 sources (`source/node-agent-coordinator/webauthn/signer.ts`, `source/electron-main/onepassword/onepassword-cli-runtime.ts`) already match binary contracts\n- **electron-main/host = artifact-fallback initially**, upgrade to clean-source only where 0.18 TS ports cleanly\n- **artifacts.json kept to strict 4-key schema** (schemaVersion/product/version/artifacts) because `tests/research-archives.test.mjs` deepEqual checks it\n- **0.44 asar identity verified twice** (analysis copy + in-DMG copy hash equal) before use\n\n## Next Steps\n1. **Phase B, step 1**: read `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs`, `scripts/build.mjs`, `scripts/lib/build-asar.mjs`, `scripts/lib/macos-package-verification.mjs`, `scripts/audit-runtime-composition.mjs` (~7.4k LOC total toolchain) to map the build contract\n2. Rework `runtimeComposition` in `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs` for 0.44 layout (drop/replace host-main entry; update preload set; deps paths from `dist/node-deps` → `dist/deps`)\n3. Rework `scripts/verify.mjs` required-list + renderer manifest checks for 0.44 (generate new `frontend/manifests/renderer-runtime-assets.json`-style inventory over 0.44 renderer assets incl. new app icon record)\n4. Run `npm run build` and iterate fail-fast on remaining 0.18-isms (`grep -rn \"0.18\" scripts/`, `dist/host`, `node-deps`, `preload-dev-controls`)\n5. Phase C source port (subsystem verdicts in `analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-delta-018-044.md` table)\n6. Phase D: package, verify, codesign; commit each increment to repo `~/Projects/active/grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed` (baseline commits: `d9271e2` import, `b3f9c86` Phase A)\n\n## Critical Context\n- **Key file paths**: new repo `/Users/panda/Projects/active/grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed/`; extracted 0.44 asar `/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/extracted/` (dist: deps, electron-main[main.cjs 12.7KB bootstrap, main-core.cjs 1.73MB, main-app.cjs 2.04MB, chrome-import-worker.cjs 13KB, proto.cjs 4.06MB], electron-preload[preload.cjs 66KB, preload-vnc.cjs 30KB, preload-webview.cjs 6.7KB], node-agent-coordinator/main.cjs 643KB, local-exec-daemon/main.cjs 3.58MB, renderer 22MB/442 assets, native, deps); DMG `/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg`; cached runtime app at `.cache/runtime/Grok Bot.app`\n- **0.44 asar package.json**: name \"sand\", version 0.44.0, main dist/electron-main/main.cjs, sandTrack \"stable\", type module, 38 `@anysphere/*` workspace deps, main.cjs bootstrap loads main-core/main-app via `vm.runInThisContext` with code-cache checks\n- **New-in-0.44 features** (no 0.18 counterpart, need fresh TS): voice-call harness (`@anysphere/grok-bot-voice-call-harness`, wss://api.x.ai/), CUGrokBotService 